> scrolls, stealing stuff with your pet ...
> 
> So I'm wondering whether it is feasible to just use shops for shopping
> only? And in the same vein: what do you (usually) do when you
> encounter a shop?

Price value *everything* in the shop with the excptions of scrolls - if
I don't have much money (you can get stuck that way) and jems.
Spellbooks you can generally find out their level, just by picking them
up - Most characters start with charisma around 10 which gives the price
of a spellbook/100 and truncated it's level. Potions can be done after
BUCing them and dipping a unicorn/quaffing uncursed ones. Rings are
difficult at the best of times as there is no sure way to ID them all
short of identify spell/scroll. Armor that costs more than standard I
usually buy if it's not a suit. If you have clairvoyance and a blindfold
(which you get *really* early), a locked shop with you in it is a very
safe place to heal as well. 

